cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use these files, cite cloth-fit's garment-data they come from and the paper it accompanies.
title: The fitted LCL skirt on FoxGirl, Gate 5 G10's drape scene
abstract: >-
  G10's scene, from Gate 8's integration run fitdrape3 (cut-8 branch,
  gates/8-loop). body.obj is Gate 8's FoxGirl fixture
  (project/fixtures/foxgirl/avatar.obj on cut-8: cloth-fit's garment-data
  assets/avatars/FoxGirl/avatar.obj, converted by
  tools/fixtures/foxgirl_convert.py: Blender (x, y, z) -> Godot (x, z, -y),
  scaled by 0.283917636 to 1.7 m, feet on y = 0), unchanged.
  fitted_skirt.obj is fit.elf's result for LCL_Skirt_DressEvening_003 on that
  body in fitdrape3 (fitdrape3.fitted.obj, body metres, the garment fixture's
  2682 vertices and 5220 triangles), rewritten with 9 decimals by
  skirt_prep.py. fitted_skirt_pins.txt is the mesh's boundary loop with the
  highest mean y (44 vertices, 0-based), as pipeline.gd picks the waist pins.
  fitted_skirt_capsules.txt is fitdrape3.json's 14 skeleton capsules (bottom,
  unit axis, radius, length in body metres; radius = median skin distance
  less 0.1 / 10, the contact offset at drape scale 10).
authors:
  - name: Zizhou Huang
  - name: The PolyFEM contributors
  - name: K. S. Ernest (iFire) Lee
